CONCLUSION:
============================================
The DMS tool has a persistent infrastructure issue preventing any conversion.
Even the simplest possible SQL statement (SELECT ProductId, Name FROM Products) fails.
All 7 statements were manually converted applying lowercase schema object names
per the transformation definition's DMS_FAILURE_MANUAL_CONVERSION_WITH_LOWERCASE_SCHEMA procedure.

Manual Conversion Rules Applied:
1. All schema object names (tables, columns, CTEs, aliases) converted to lowercase
2. SCOPE_IDENTITY() -> RETURNING clause
3. GETDATE() -> NOW()
4. DECLARE/SET variable pattern -> PostgreSQL DO $$ block or inline approach
5. BEGIN TRANSACTION/COMMIT -> restructured for PostgreSQL compatibility
6. Integer division handled with CAST for ROUND operations
7. Window functions (LAG, RANK, PERCENT_RANK, AVG/MIN/MAX OVER) preserved as-is (PostgreSQL compatible)
8. CASE expressions preserved as-is (PostgreSQL compatible)
9. BETWEEN preserved as-is (PostgreSQL compatible)
